[Event "Nimzo-Indian: Rubinstein 4.e3"]

{The Nimzo-Indian (3...Bb4) pins the c3-knight to stop e4. Black is willing to give up the bishop pair to double White's c-pawns.}
1. d4 {Centre. The pawn on d4 controls e5.}
1... Nf6 {Flexible. The knight on f6 controls d5 and e4.}
2. c4 {Space. The pawn on c4 controls d5.}
2... e6 {Prepares ...Bb4. The pawn on e6 controls d5.}
3. Nc3 {Prepares e4. The knight on c3 controls d5 and e4.}
3... Bb4 {[%cal Gb4c3] The Nimzo: pins the knight and stops e4.}
4. e3 {The Rubinstein.}
4... O-O {Castles. The king is safe and the rook comes into play.}
 (4... c5 {Strikes d4 at once. The pawn on c5 eyes the pawn on d4.}
5. Bd3 {Develops. The bishop on d3 eyes the pawn on h7 and controls e4.}
5... Nc6 {More pressure on d4. The knight on c6 eyes the pawn on d4 and controls e5.}
6. Nf3 {Develops. The knight on f3 controls e5.}
6... Bxc3+ {Doubles the c-pawns. The bishop on c3 eyes the pawn on d4 and the pawn on b2. It is check, so the reply is forced.}
7. bxc3 {Recaptures toward the centre.}
7... d6 {The Hübner plan: ...e5 and a dark-square blockade against the doubled pawns.}
)
5. Bd3 {Develops. The bishop on d3 eyes the pawn on h7 and controls e4.}
5... d5 {Centre. The pawn on d5 eyes the pawn on c4 and controls e4.}
6. Nf3 {Develops. The knight on f3 controls e5.}
6... c5 {Hits d4. The pawn on c5 eyes the pawn on d4.}
7. O-O {Castles. The king is safe and the rook comes into play.}
7... dxc4 {Takes. The pawn on c4 eyes the bishop on d3.}
8. Bxc4 {Recaptures. The bishop on c4 eyes the pawn on e6 and controls d5.}
8... Nc6 {Develops. The knight on c6 eyes the pawn on d4 and controls e5.}
9. a3 {Asks the bishop. The pawn on a3 eyes the bishop on b4.}
9... Ba5 {Keeps the pin. The bishop on a5 eyes the knight on c3.} *

[Event "Nimzo-Indian: Classical, Sämisch & Leningrad"]

{4.Qc2 avoids doubled pawns, 4.f3 prepares e4, 4.Bg5 pins.}
1. d4 {Centre. The pawn on d4 controls e5.}
1... Nf6 {Flexible. The knight on f6 controls d5 and e4.}
2. c4 {Space. The pawn on c4 controls d5.}
2... e6 {Prepares ...Bb4. The pawn on e6 controls d5.}
3. Nc3 {Develops. The knight on c3 controls d5 and e4.}
3... Bb4 {Nimzo. The bishop on b4 eyes the knight on c3.}
4. Qc2 {The Classical. The queen on c2 eyes the pawn on h7 and controls e4.}
 (4. f3 {Prepares e4. The pawn on f3 controls e4.}
4... d5 {Stops e4. The pawn on d5 eyes the pawn on c4 and controls e4.}
5. a3 {Asks the bishop. The pawn on a3 eyes the bishop on b4.}
5... Be7 {Keeps the bishop. The bishop on e7 eyes the pawn on a3.}
6. e4 {Centre. The pawn on e4 eyes the pawn on d5.}
6... dxe4 {Takes. The pawn on e4 eyes the pawn on f3.}
7. fxe4 {Recaptures. The pawn on e4 controls d5.}
7... e5 {Strikes. The pawn on e5 eyes the pawn on d4.}
8. d5 {Gains space.}
8... Bc5 {Active. The bishop on c5 eyes the pawn on a3 and the knight on g1 and controls d4.}
)
 (4. Bg5 {The Leningrad. The bishop on g5 eyes the knight on f6.}
4... h6 {Asks the bishop. The pawn on h6 eyes the bishop on g5.}
5. Bh4 {Keeps the pin. The bishop on h4 eyes the knight on f6.}
5... c5 {Hits d4. The pawn on c5 eyes the pawn on d4.}
6. d5 {Gains space. The pawn on d5 eyes the pawn on e6.}
6... d6 {Solid. The pawn on d6 controls e5.}
)
4... O-O {Castles. The king is safe and the rook comes into play.}
5. a3 {Asks the bishop. The pawn on a3 eyes the bishop on b4.}
5... Bxc3+ {Takes. The bishop on c3 eyes the pawn on d4 and the pawn on b2. It is check, so the reply is forced.}
6. Qxc3 {Recaptures.}
6... b6 {Fianchetto.}
7. Bg5 {Pins. The bishop on g5 eyes the knight on f6.}
7... Bb7 {Develops. The bishop on b7 eyes the pawn on g2 and controls d5 and e4.}
8. f3 {Stops ...Ne4. The pawn on f3 controls e4.}
8... h6 {Asks. The pawn on h6 eyes the bishop on g5.}
9. Bh4 {Keeps the pin. The bishop on h4 eyes the knight on f6.}
9... d5 {Centre. The pawn on d5 eyes the pawn on c4 and controls e4.} *
